From 9d481b0b2f80532835975b47c5e77d8307fc88a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hank Yeomans <hank@quorra.ah.local>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 09:45:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 47/54] dsv41 engram file layout: hash and fetch the chunked
 request's next prefill chunk from the post-hasher break (recipe T3.20 (c))

SGLANG_DSV41_ENGRAM_CHUNK_AHEAD (default on): the scheduler hands each extend
batch that continues a chunked request its next chunk's tokens and n-1
predecessors (ForwardBatch.engram_next_chunk); the post-hasher break hashes
them with the same extend kernel (no history commit) and queues both tables'
rows behind the current chunk's on the shared worker. _FileTable keeps the
chunk-ahead fetch in its own slot so interleaved decode steps do not evict it,
adopts it on the next chunk's submit when its ids are a prefix (the last chunk
is shorter), and reports chunk-ahead hit/dropped in the stats line.

Amp-Thread-ID: https://ampcode.com/threads/T-01a0c10b-a5f8-77fc-b238-7147d12ccf29
Co-authored-by: Amp <amp@ampcode.com>
